# corpus-pcode/NOTICES

Each program in `corpus-pcode/` is a P-code build of a program in `corpus/`.
It is here because the licence of its source permits redistribution.

The author built each one on a Windows XP host with the Visual Basic 6 IDE
(VB6 SP6, `VB6.EXE` of 1,895,424 bytes, dated 2004-02-23), from the corpus
project of the same path, with one change: in the project file, the line
`CompilationType=0` became `CompilationType=-1`. Nothing else was changed.
`cargo run -p xtask -- export-pcode` makes that change, and
`cargo run -p xtask -- import-pcode` copies each executable here.

`tests/pcode.toml` gives, for each program, the hash of the corpus files that
the build read, the result of the build, and the SHA-256 of the executable.
The source of each executable is in this repository, in `corpus/`, at the
commit that adds the executable.

